SQLite 3.7.6.3 source, trimmed to what the build needs

sqlite-src-3070603/ is the official source archive, unchanged:
https://www.sqlite.org/sqlite-src-3070603.zip
(sha256 f40dbcfed53853727cec0135b527d209170f8703c1013b24d066a0df9b82cdc9)

The build runs configure and generates the parser, keyword hash and amalgamation
from it with Sony's options, so the configure files, src/, tool/ and ext/ (the
amalgamation lists the extension sources) are kept. Left out: test/, art/, doc/,
contrib/, the other platforms' makefiles (Makefile.arm-wince-mingw32ce-gcc,
Makefile.linux-gcc, Makefile.vxworks), the publish and DLL scripts (publish.sh,
publish_osx.sh, mkdll.sh, mkextu.sh, mkextw.sh, mkso.sh) and spec.template. Every kept
file is identical to the archive.

The upstream VERSION file identifies release 3.7.6.3. The upstream README and
public-domain notices in the source files are retained. The enclosing vendor
directory keeps LICENSE and the official sqlite3.h; the official amalgamation
(sqlite3.c) is left out, since the build generates its own.

Generate configured parsers and amalgamations in build directories. Sony changes
belong to the consuming module's separate patches or explicitly marked SCE code.
